From: Loong <1031313955@qq.com>
Subject: [PATCH] configs: nokia_xg-040g-md: enable minimal HTTP recovery server

Turns on the TCP stack and the httpd command added by
202-net-add-minimal-httpd-server.patch, plus the cyclic framework it uses to
keep the panel LEDs blinking during a flash write (the SPI-NAND layer calls
schedule() once per page, which is what drives it).

HTTPD_FACTORY_VOLS names the two per-unit volumes the ubi layout keeps
(ubi_create_board_data in the defenv: ri holds the factory MAC at +0x3e,
bosa the optics calibration, 0x40000 each), so the page can offer to
restore them from a backup with an exact-size check.

CMD_HTTPD_STOCK_RESTORE opts this board into the raw flash write.  The
stock all_flash.bin is 0xEBA0000 bytes and starts at offset 0; the page
checks nothing beyond "fits the chip".

Must sort after 401-add-nokia-xg-040g-md.patch, which is the patch that
creates this defconfig in the first place.

--- a/configs/an7581_nokia_xg-040g-md_defconfig
+++ b/configs/an7581_nokia_xg-040g-md_defconfig
@@ -41,6 +41,11 @@
 CONFIG_CMD_MTD_NAND_WRITE_TEST=y
 CONFIG_CMD_PART=y
 CONFIG_CMD_TFTPSRV=y
+CONFIG_PROT_TCP=y
+CONFIG_CMD_HTTPD=y
+CONFIG_HTTPD_FACTORY_VOLS="ri:0x40000 bosa:0x40000"
+CONFIG_CMD_HTTPD_STOCK_RESTORE=y
+CONFIG_CYCLIC=y
 CONFIG_CMD_RARP=y
 CONFIG_CMD_CDP=y
 CONFIG_CMD_SNTP=y
